  "articleBody": "Repainting a room will not hide underlying wall problems for long. Calling in a skilled professional is the smart move when your walls show these warning signs:\n\n- Peeling or Flaking Wall Paint: When paint separates from the drywall core, rolling over it creates jagged ridges and eventual peeling across the entire surface.\n- Flashing and Dull Patches: If past touch-ups left obvious dull spots across the wall, the surface porosity is uneven and requires proper sealing and uniform topcoats.\n- Textured Wall Repairs: Matching existing knockdown, orange peel, or hand-troweled drywall texture after a repair requires specialized tools and finish experience.\n- Deep or Widespread Wall Cracks: Settling cracks that reappear need joint tape and drywall compound repairs, not just a thin layer of paint.\n- Suspected Lead Paint in Pre-1978 Properties: Scraping or power sanding walls in older homes demands certified lead-safe work practices and dust containment.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps: Bringing in an experienced contractor ensures the drywall underneath is structurally sound, clean, and properly primed before the finish coats go on.\n\nReady to resolve your wall issues the right way? Contact Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 for dependable drywall repair and wall painting services.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
